 793:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c **** 
 794:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c **** /****************************************************************************
 795:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * Build a list of the current bindings for the device address binding      *
 796:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * property as required for the ReadsRange functionality.                   *
 797:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * We assume we only get called for "Read All" or "By Position" requests.   *
 798:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  *                                                                          *
 799:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * We need to treat the address cache as a contiguous array but in reality  *
 800:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * it could be sparsely populated. We can get the count but we can only     *
 801:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * extract entries by doing a linear scan starting from the first entry in  *
 802:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * the cache and picking them off one by one.                               *
 803:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  *                                                                          *
 804:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * We do assume the list cannot change whilst we are accessing it so would  *
 805:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * not be multithread safe if there are other tasks that change the cache.  *
 806:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  *                                                                          *
 807:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * We take the simple approach here to filling the buffer by taking a max   *
 808:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * size for a single entry and then stopping if there is less than that     *
 809:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * left in the buffer. You could build each entry in a seperate buffer and  *
 810:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * determine the exact length before copying but this is time consuming,    *
 811:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * requires more memory and would probably only let you sqeeeze one more    *
 812:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * entry in on occasion. The value is calculated as 5 bytes for the device  *
 813:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/address.c ****  * ID + 3 bytes for the network number and nine bytes for the MAC address   *
